 * File Description:
 *
 * This file is included into GKI files to generate the KiSignalBaseId enumeration.
 *
 * Any extra terminal client signal bases can be defined within this file. These
 * bases will be added to the EX signal set (this file is included into EXSIGSET.H).
 *
 * Bases should be added in the following way:
 *
 * KI_BASE_DEF (EX1)
 * KI_BASE_DEF (EX2)
 * KI_BASE_DEF (EX3)
 * KI_BASE_DEF (EX4)
 *
 * The base name does not need to start with EX but it is best to use a prefix that
 * will help guarantee a unique id within the whole of the GKI system.
 *
 * The KI_BASE_DEF() macro adds _SIGNAL_BASE to the end of the parameter
 * given as the base name. This is done to enforce the GKI naming convention.
