/*******************************************************************************
* Macro       : KI_SEMA_DEF
* Group       : GKI, Config
* Parameter   : sEMAiD = This is the id that will be added to the KiSemaphoreId
*                   enumeration. This is what the application code will use to
*                   reference a semaphore in any of the semaphore related GKI
*                   functions.
* Parameter   : int iNITIALcOUNT = This is the initial count that the GKI should
*                   set for the semaphore at boot time.
* Returns     : Nothing
* Description : This macro is used to define a GKI semaphore. The macro is
*                   redefined several times within the GKI to create data types
*                   and storage to support the defined semaphores. The GKI will
*                   create the semaphore and set it's count at boot time.
*                   Applications use the given semaphore id (sEMAiD parameter)
*                   when calling any semaphore related GKI functions.
*******************************************************************************/




/*******************************************************************************
* Macro       : KI_SEMA_RESERVED
* Group       : GKI, Config
* Parameter   : sEMAiD = This is the id that will be added to the KiSemaphoreId
*                   enumeration.
* Returns     : Nothing
* Description : This macro is used to reserve a location in the GKI semaphore
*                   id table. The reserved id cannot be used in a GKI semaphore
*                   function as the semaphore will not exist (this will cause an
*                   assert). This is mainly used to maintain the numbering of
*                   semaphore id's when some are dependent on conditional
*                   compiles.
*******************************************************************************/




/***************************************************************************
* SEMAPHORES SHOULD NOT BE USED WHERE POSSIBLE. THE MAIN INTERTASK
* COMMUNICATION AND SYNCHRONISATION SHOULD BE DONE USING GKI SIGNALS.
* SEMAPHORES ARE CURRENTLY NOT LOGGED AND THERE CAN BE PROBLEMS WHEN USING
* BOTH SIGNALS AND SEMAPHORES IN THE SAME TASK.
*
* ONLY ADD SEMAPHORES TO THE END OF THE LIST OR USE OLD REDUNDANT ENTRIES.
* IF A SEMAPHORE IS NO LONGER NEEDED REPLACE IT WITH A REDUNDANT ENTRY
* RATHER THAN REMOVING IT. THE NUMBERING OF THE SEMAPHORE ID'S MUST BE KEPT
* THE SAME.
*
* IF A SEMAPHORE IS CONDITIONALLY COMPILED ADD A RESERVED ENTRY IN AN
* ELSE CONDITION SO THAT THE NUMBERING DOES NOT CHANGE BASED ON CONDITIONAL
* COMPILES.
***************************************************************************/

/***************************************************************************
